From: Vylen Linux Team
Date: 2026-08-22
Subject: [PATCH] adb: avoid Protobuf 36 / Abseil LOG macro conflict

Protobuf 36.0 includes Abseil logging headers that define a global LOG macro.
That macro can override Android base logging in ADB translation units and makes
LOG(DEBUG) expand to an unsupported Abseil severity. The resulting build errors
include "STATELESS was not declared" and
"ABSL_LOG_INTERNAL_CONDITION_DEBUG was not declared".

Avoid the colliding generic LOG macro in the affected ADB debug paths by using
ADB_LOG, which expands directly through Android logging's LOGGING_PREAMBLE and
LOG_STREAM helpers. This preserves the intended Android DEBUG logging even after
Protobuf-generated headers have included Abseil.

Fixes: android-tools 37.0.0 build with Protobuf 36.0
---
--- a/vendor/adb/adb_trace.h
+++ b/vendor/adb/adb_trace.h
@@ -49,11 +49,15 @@ enum AdbTrace {
 #define VLOG_IS_ON(TAG) \
     ((adb_trace_mask & (1 << (TAG))) != 0)

+// Do not use the generic LOG macro here: Protobuf 36 brings in Abseil,
+// which exports another macro with the same name.
+#define ADB_LOG(severity) LOGGING_PREAMBLE(severity) && LOG_STREAM(severity)
+
 #define VLOG(TAG)                 \
     if (LIKELY(!VLOG_IS_ON(TAG))) \
         ;                         \
     else                          \
-        LOG(DEBUG)
+        ADB_LOG(DEBUG)

 // You must define TRACE_TAG before using this macro.
 #define D(...) \
--- a/vendor/adb/transport.cpp
+++ b/vendor/adb/transport.cpp
@@ -1675,7 +1675,7 @@ void atransport::UpdateReverseConfig(std::string_view config) {

         if (norebind && reverse_forwards_.contains(remote)) {
             // This will fail, don't update the map.
-            LOG(DEBUG) << "ignoring reverse forward that will fail due to norebind";
+            ADB_LOG(DEBUG) << "ignoring reverse forward that will fail due to norebind";
             return;
         }

@@ -1691,7 +1691,7 @@ void atransport::UpdateReverseConfig(std::string_view config) {
     } else if (service_addr == "killforward-all") {
         reverse_forwards_.clear();
     } else if (service_addr == "list-forward") {
-        LOG(DEBUG) << __func__ << " ignoring --list";
+        ADB_LOG(DEBUG) << __func__ << " ignoring --list";
     } else {  // Anything else we need to know about?
         LOG(FATAL) << "unhandled reverse service: " << service_addr;
     }
